<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>texture</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The texture to apply to the quad. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>model</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The model matrix (position, rotation, scale). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>view</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The view matrix (camera position). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>projection</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The projection matrix (orthographic or perspective). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>tileScaleX</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Number of texture repetitions along the X axis (default: 1.0). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>tileScaleY</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Number of texture repetitions along the Y axis (default: 1.0).</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
This is the primary rendering method for 2D sprites. It applies the model, view, and projection matrices to position the quad in world space, and uses a tile scale to repeat the texture across the quad surface.</para>
